      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that they have different priorities, but you mentioned that restorative approaches \"better align\" with justice as fairness. doesn't that kind of imply that retributive justice is inherently less aligned with modern justice or even fundamentally flawed in how it handles systemic issues? like, isn't one objectively more \"evolved\" in a modern context?",
